    "title": "Activities",
    "to": "/docs/Activities-Module/activities",
    "description": "Learn how to manage tasks and smart nudges from the Activities module.",
    "body": "Activities The Activities module provides a centralized workspace for managing all CRM related activities across Leads, Deals, Contacts, and Organizations . It consolidates tasks and AI generated smart nudges into a single location, enabling users to track, prioritize, and complete activities efficiently without navigating between individual records. Activities created from this module are automatically linked to their associated CRM records and are reflected throughout the system, ensuring consistent activity tracking and visibility. Activities Workspace The Activities page displays all assigned activities in a unified list view and allows users to: View all tasks and smart nudges in one place. Monitor upcoming and overdue activities. Create new tasks. Search and filter activities. Sort activities by Due Date , Priority , and Recent . Access activities associated with Leads, Deals, Contacts, or Organizations. Mark important activities for quick access. Activity Tabs The Activities workspace is divided into three tabs. All Activities Displays all activities assigned to the user, including both manually created tasks and AI generated smart nudges. This view provides a complete overview of pending work and recommended actions across the CRM. Tasks Displays only manually created tasks. Use this tab when you want to focus exclusively on planned follow ups, calls, meetings, reminders, or other user created activities. Smart Nudges Displays AI generated recommendations that help users take timely actions on CRM records. Examples include: Lead has not been contacted recently. Deal value has increased. Follow up is overdue. Customer engagement has declined. Smart Nudges help ensure that important opportunities and actions are not overlooked. Filtering Activities Activities can be filtered to quickly locate relevant records. Available filters include: Status Filter Filter activities based on their current status. Examples may include: Pending In Progress Completed Overdue Date Filter Filter activities based on due dates or activity dates. Priority Filter Filter activities according to their assigned priority level. Low Medium High Multiple filters can be applied simultaneously to narrow results. Searching Activities The Activities module includes a search feature that allows users to quickly locate activities. Users can search using: Activity title Associated record name Keywords within the activity Search results update dynamically as text is entered. Creating a Task Tasks can be created directly from the Activities module. Steps 1. Click New Task . 2. Complete the task details. 3. Click Submit . The task is immediately added to: The Activities list. The associated Lead, Deal, Contact, or Organization record.",
