    "label": "Calendar",
    "title": "Calendar",
    "to": "/docs/Calendar-Module/calendar",
    "description": "Learn how to manage meetings and schedules using the Calendar module.",
    "body": "Calendar The Calendar module provides a visual scheduling interface for managing CRM activities. It displays tasks and meetings in a calendar format, allowing users to plan work, monitor upcoming commitments, and track activity schedules across Leads, Deals, Contacts, and Organizations . All activities created within the CRM are automatically reflected in the Calendar, providing a centralized view of scheduled work. Calendar Views The Calendar supports multiple viewing modes to accommodate different planning needs. Day View Displays activities scheduled for a single day. This view is useful for managing daily workloads and appointments. Week View Displays activities across an entire week. This view helps users plan upcoming tasks, meetings, and follow ups over several days. Month View Displays activities for the entire month. This view provides a high level overview of upcoming commitments and workload distribution. Calendar Sidebar The left hand panel provides quick access to scheduling information. Mini Calendar Allows users to quickly jump to a specific date. Today's Meetings Displays meetings scheduled for the current day. This section helps users quickly identify upcoming commitments without navigating through the calendar. Creating Meetings Users can schedule meetings directly from the Calendar module. Steps 1. Navigate to Calendar . 2. Click New . 3. Enter the meeting details. 4. Select the related CRM record ( Lead, Deal, Contact, or Organization , if applicable). 5. Specify the meeting date and time. 6. Click Save . Once created, the meeting is automatically added to: The Calendar view. The Global Activities section. The associated Lead, Deal, Contact, or Organization record. This ensures that all participants and related records have visibility into the scheduled meeting. Benefits The Calendar module helps users: Visualize scheduled meetings and activities. Plan daily, weekly, and monthly workloads. Keep track of upcoming commitments. Schedule meetings directly from a centralized interface. Access meetings associated with Leads, Deals, Contacts, and Organizations. Improve collaboration and time management across the sales team.",
