    "description": "Learn how to configure calling providers and manage call activity in SalesAstra.",
    "body": "Call Settings The Call Settings section allows administrators to configure calling providers and manage call records generated through SalesAstra. It provides a centralized location to: Connect and manage calling service providers. Review call activity. Access call recordings. View call summaries and notes. Convert eligible calls into Leads. Navigate to associated Lead records. Call Settings includes: Providers Call Logs Providers The Providers section allows administrators to connect and manage supported calling service providers used with SalesAstra. The Providers page displays the available providers along with their connection and availability status. Provider Overview The page provides summary information such as: Total Providers – Total number of calling providers available. Connected – Number of providers currently connected. Active – Number of active providers. Total Numbers – Total number of phone numbers configured with the providers. Default Caller ID – The caller ID configured for outgoing calls. Provider Status Providers can display different statuses based on their configuration: Connected / Disconnected – Indicates whether the provider is connected to SalesAstra. Active / Disabled – Indicates whether the provider is enabled for calling. Connecting a Provider To connect a calling provider: 1. Go to Call Settings → Providers . 2. Locate the required provider. 3. Click Connect . 4. Enter the required provider configuration or credentials. 5. Complete the connection process. Once connected and active, the provider can be used for calling based on its configuration. Filtering Providers You can filter providers using the available options: All Providers Connected Active Not Connected You can also use Search Providers to find a specific provider. Call Logs The Call Logs section provides a centralized view of calls made or received through the configured calling providers. Call Logs allow users to: View call records. Search for calls. Filter calls by date or provider. Play available recordings. View call summaries and notes. Convert eligible calls into Leads. Open associated Leads. For detailed information, see Call Logs .",
