    "label": "Contact Details",
    "title": "Contact Details",
    "to": "/docs/Contacts-Module/contact-details",
    "description": "Learn about the Contact Details page and its features.",
    "body": "Contact Details The Contact Detail page provides a centralized view of all information, interactions, and relationships associated with a Contact. It enables users to manage contact information, track engagement history, create follow up activities, and monitor related business records such as Leads and Deals from a single location. The page is divided into multiple sections and tabs that help users maintain a complete view of customer interactions and ongoing opportunities. Contact Overview The left panel displays the Contact's profile information and key details, including: Contact Name Email Address Contact Owner Source Engagement Status Phone Numbers Company Information Communication Details Additional Information This information is displayed according to the fields configured by the administrator for the organization. Contact Actions The Contact Detail page provides quick action buttons that allow users to perform common CRM activities without leaving the Contact record. Available actions include: Edit Contact Create Note Create Task Create Deal Log Activity These actions can also be performed from their respective tabs where applicable. Edit Contact Use the Edit Contact option to update existing Contact information. Steps 1. Open the Contact Detail page. 2. Click the Edit icon. 3. Modify the required fields. 4. Click Save . Any changes made are reflected immediately in the Contact record. Activity Timeline Logged activities automatically appear in the Contact's Activity Timeline , ensuring a complete record of interactions is maintained. The timeline provides a chronological view of all activities associated with the Contact, allowing users to quickly review customer interactions and follow up history. Activities that appear in the timeline may include: Notes Tasks Meetings Emails Logged Activities Deal Creation Other CRM events This centralized timeline helps sales teams maintain complete visibility into customer engagement throughout the relationship. Contact Detail Tabs The Contact Detail page also includes dedicated tabs for managing related information. Activities Displays the chronological history of interactions, updates, tasks, notes, and other CRM activities associated with the Contact. Notes Displays all notes created for the Contact and allows users to create and manage additional notes. Tasks Displays all tasks associated with the Contact and allows users to create and manage follow up activities. Linked Deals Displays all Deals associated with the Contact, allowing users to monitor active opportunities, review deal progress, and access Deal records directly from the Contact profile. Linked Leads Displays all Leads associated with the Contact, helping users understand the Contact's acquisition journey, review Lead history, and access Lead records directly from the Contact profile. Note Each of the above sections is documented in detail within its respective page in this guide.",
