    "description": "Learn how to create and manage notes associated with Contacts.",
    "body": "Notes The Notes feature allows users to capture important information, meeting summaries, customer discussions, observations, and follow up details related to a Contact. Notes help maintain a complete history of customer interactions, making it easier for team members to understand the context of conversations and collaborate effectively throughout the customer relationship. Accessing Notes 1. Navigate to the Contacts module. 2. Open the required Contact record. 3. Go to the Notes tab under the Activities section. 4. Click Create Note . This opens the Note Editor . Creating a Note After opening the Note Editor: 1. Enter the note content using the rich text editor. 2. Format the content as required. 3. Optionally: Create a follow up reminder. Create a To Do item associated with the note. 4. Click Submit . The note is automatically associated with the Contact and becomes visible in both the Activity Timeline and Notes tab. Note Features The Notes feature provides the following capabilities: Rich text formatting support. Follow up reminders. To Do creation from notes. Automatic association with the Contact record. Visibility within the Contact Timeline and Notes tab. Managing Notes Users can perform the following actions on existing notes: View notes. Edit notes. Delete notes. Search notes. Pin important notes. Viewing Notes All notes are displayed in chronological order under the Notes tab. Each note displays: Author Date and Time Note Content This provides complete visibility into discussions and updates throughout the customer lifecycle. Benefits The Notes feature helps users: Maintain conversation history. Record meeting outcomes. Capture customer requirements. Preserve important contextual information. Improve collaboration among team members. Maintain a complete history of customer interactions. Best Practices Record customer discussions immediately after meetings or calls. Keep notes clear and concise. Include important decisions and action items. Update notes whenever new information becomes available. Use notes to maintain a complete history of customer interactions.",
