    "label": "Tasks",
    "title": "Tasks",
    "to": "/docs/Contacts-Module/tasks",
    "description": "Learn how to create and manage tasks associated with Contacts.",
    "body": "Tasks The Tasks feature helps users schedule, assign, and track follow up activities related to a Contact. Tasks ensure that important customer interactions are completed on time and help sales teams stay organized throughout the customer lifecycle. Tasks can be created from: The Create Task action button in the Contact profile panel. The Tasks tab under the Activities section. Creating a Task Steps 1. Navigate to the Contacts module. 2. Open the required Contact record. 3. Go to the Tasks tab or click Create Task from the Contact Details page. 4. Enter the required task information. 5. Click Submit . The task is automatically associated with the selected Contact. Task Information While creating a task, users can configure the following details: Field Description Task Title Name of the task. Task Type Type of activity to be performed. Status Current task status. Priority Priority level of the task. Due Date & Time Scheduled completion date and time. Assigned User User responsible for completing the task. Contributors Additional users collaborating on the task. Description Additional information or instructions related to the task. Task Features The Tasks feature provides the following capabilities: Assign tasks to team members. Set due dates and times. Define task priorities. Add contributors. Track task completion status. Task Status Tasks can be managed using different statuses depending on their progress. Common task statuses include: Open In Progress Completed Overdue Task Priorities Users can assign priorities to help organize work efficiently. Common priority levels include: Low Medium High Managing Tasks Users can perform the following actions: View tasks. Edit task details. Update task status. Mark tasks as completed. Delete tasks when no longer required. All updates are automatically reflected in the Contact's Activity Timeline . Benefits The Tasks feature helps users: Ensure timely customer follow ups. Improve accountability. Coordinate activities among team members. Prevent missed customer engagements. Maintain a complete record of follow up activities. Best Practices Create tasks immediately after customer interactions. Assign realistic due dates. Update task status regularly. Use priorities to focus on critical follow ups. Review pending tasks frequently to ensure timely completion.",
