    "label": "Manager Dashboard",
    "title": "Manager Dashboard",
    "to": "/docs/Dashboard/manager-dashboard",
    "description": "Learn how the Manager Dashboard helps sales managers monitor team pipeline, conversion, risks, targets, and source performance.",
    "body": "Manager Dashboard The Manager Dashboard provides sales managers with a centralized view of team pipeline performance, conversion, sales risks, individual sales performance, target achievement, and lead source effectiveness. It is designed to help managers monitor their team's sales performance, identify pipeline risks, track progress against targets, and take timely action from a single workspace. The Manager Dashboard is assigned to users through Role Management . Users can also customize the Dashboard by showing or hiding available sections. Dashboard Sections 1. Pipeline Stats The Pipeline Stats section provides a quick overview of the team's active sales pipeline. Metrics Displayed Total Pipeline Value – Total value of active Deals in the pipeline. Total Active Deals – Number of active Deals. Average Deal Size – Average value of active Deals. The section also displays the number of pipeline stages represented in the current data. 2. Stage Distribution The Stage Distribution section shows how the team's pipeline value is distributed across Deal stages. The visualization provides a breakdown of: Deal Stage Number of Deals Pipeline Value Percentage of Total Pipeline Examples of stages may include: Opportunity Discovery Property Recommendation Site Visit Scheduled Site Visit Completed Pricing Discussion Booking Commitment Other Managers can use this information to understand where Deals are concentrated within the pipeline. Clicking a stage can open the corresponding filtered Deal records. 3. Pipeline by Rep The Pipeline by Rep section provides a sales representative level view of the active pipeline. Information Displayed Sales Representative Pipeline Share % Number of Deals Pipeline Amount The section allows managers to identify how pipeline value is distributed across individual sales representatives. Clicking a representative can provide access to the relevant performance or Deal information, subject to permissions. 4. Conversion Funnel The Conversion Funnel provides a visual representation of the team's sales conversion process. The funnel can show progression through stages such as: Leads → Qualified Leads → Deals → Won Managers can use the funnel to understand: Number of Leads entering the funnel Number of Qualified Leads Number of Deals created Number of Won Deals Drop off between stages This helps provide a high level view of conversion performance. 5. Risk & Alerts The Risk & Alerts section identifies Deals or sales conditions that may require manager attention. Managers can view alerts across categories such as: All Alerts Deals Activity Rep Risks Example Alerts Stage stuck Close date passed Deal inactivity Aging Deal Pipeline risk Sales representative risk Each alert may display: Record or sales representative Number of risks detected Risk type Priority Age or duration Alert time Available Actions Depending on the alert, managers can: View – Open the relevant record or details. Assign – Assign the item to a user. Remind – Create or trigger a reminder for follow up. 6. Team Performance Leaderboard The Team Performance Leaderboard provides a comparative view of sales representative performance within the manager's team. The leaderboard can display: Rank Sales Representative Revenue Number of Deals Conversion % Activities Completed Managers can select the metric used for ranking, such as Revenue Closed . The section may also highlight the top performers separately for quick visibility. :::note Rankings are calculated using the selected performance metric and reporting period. ::: 7. Target Achievement The Target Achievement section compares sales performance against configured targets. The visualization can compare target and achieved values for relevant Deals, teams, or business units. Managers can use this section to monitor: Target value Achieved value Achievement percentage Performance against target The available data depends on the configured targets and the user's access permissions. 8. Source Performance Analy",
