    "label": "Dashboard",
    "title": "Dashboard",
    "to": "/docs/Dashboard/overview",
    "description": "Learn how to use and customize the SalesAstra Dashboard, including role-based dashboards, sales performance, pipeline insights, targets, and AI-powered recommendations.",
    "body": "Dashboard The Dashboard provides a centralized view of sales activities, pipeline information, performance metrics, targets, and AI powered recommendations. It enables users to monitor important information and take action without navigating through multiple modules. The Dashboard displayed to a user is determined by the Dashboard assigned to their role . Administrators can configure which type of Dashboard is available for each role while defining or editing the role. Users can further personalize their assigned Dashboard by choosing which sections they want to display. Configure a Dashboard for a Role 1. Navigate to Settings . 2. Open Roles and Permissions . 3. Create a new role or open an existing role for editing. 4. Select the required Dashboard . 5. Save the role configuration. 6. Assign the role to the required users. Users assigned to the role will see the configured dashboard when they access SalesAstra. Dashboard Customization The Dashboard is customizable, allowing users to show only the sections that are relevant to their day to day work. Customize Dashboard To customize the Dashboard: 1. Navigate to Dashboard . 2. Click Customize Dashboard . 3. The Customize Dashboard panel opens. 4. Review the available Dashboard sections. 5. Use the toggle beside a section to enable or disable it. 6. Enable the sections you want to display on your Dashboard. 7. Disable sections that are not required. Available sections may include: My Day Smart Nudges Mini Funnel Pipeline by Stage My Performance Weekly Revenue Activity Breakdown The Dashboard automatically reflects the selected configuration. Hide a Section Directly Users can also hide a section directly from the Dashboard. 1. Locate the section you want to hide. 2. Click the Eye icon in the section header. 3. A confirmation message is displayed. 4. Click Hide . The section is removed from the Dashboard but is not deleted. It can be enabled again from Customize Dashboard . :::note Hiding a Dashboard section only changes the user's Dashboard view. It does not remove the underlying data or functionality. ::: Reset Dashboard If required, users can restore the Dashboard to its default section configuration. 1. Open Customize Dashboard . 2. Click Reset . 3. The Dashboard sections are restored to their default visibility. Types of Dashboards SalesAstra supports different Dashboard configurations based on the user's role. Administrators can select the Dashboard that should be available to a role while configuring the role. The available Dashboard types include: Sales Representative Dashboard Leadership Dashboard Manager Dashboard The Dashboard type determines the information and widgets available to the user. Individual users can then customize the visibility of the available sections according to their requirements.",
