    "body": "Sales Representative Dashboard The Sales Representative Dashboard provides a centralized workspace where sales representatives can view their daily priorities, monitor their Deal pipeline, track performance, and act on AI generated suggestions. The Dashboard is fully customizable, allowing sales representatives to display only the sections that are relevant to their day to day activities. Dashboard Overview The Sales Representative Dashboard includes the following sections: My Day Smart Nudges Total Deals Total Pipeline Value Mini Funnel Pipeline by Stage My Performance Weekly Revenue Activity Breakdown The sections displayed on the Dashboard may vary depending on the user's Dashboard configuration. My Day The My Day section provides a consolidated view of the sales representative's daily priorities. It brings together tasks, follow ups, and meetings so that users can manage their daily activities without navigating to multiple modules. Information Displayed The section can display: Task or activity title Related Lead or Deal Activity type Due time Priority Current status Priority can be indicated as: High Medium Low Available Actions Depending on the activity type, users can: Mark as Complete for tasks Join scheduled meetings Open the related Lead or Deal View activity details Overdue activities are highlighted to help users identify items requiring immediate attention. Smart Nudges The Smart Nudges section displays AI powered suggestions intended to help sales representatives take timely actions. Examples include: Clarify pricing questions with a customer Send a detailed cost sheet Create a follow up task Schedule a site visit Each nudge includes an Act option where applicable. Selecting Act allows the user to perform the suggested action directly or navigate to the relevant functionality. Total Deals The Total Deals card displays the number of Deals currently included in the user's pipeline. It may also indicate the number of pipeline stages containing those Deals. Total Pipeline Value The Total Pipeline Value card displays the combined value of the user's active Deals. The value is displayed using the organization's configured currency. Where applicable, the widget may also indicate whether the value represents a weighted forecast. Mini Funnel The Mini Funnel provides a simplified visual representation of Deals progressing through the sales pipeline. It displays the number of Deals at each stage, allowing users to quickly understand how Deals are distributed from early stages toward closure. For example: Discovery Site Visit Scheduled Site Visit Completed Pricing Discussion Booking Commitment Filters Users can apply available filters such as: Fiscal Year Pipeline or applicable Deal property The funnel updates based on the selected filter values. Pipeline by Stage The Pipeline by Stage section provides a stage wise view of the user's active Deal pipeline. Each stage can display: Number of Deals Total Deal Value Percentage of the overall pipeline The visualization provides a quick understanding of where Deals are concentrated. View Deals by Stage Select a pipeline stage to view the corresponding Deals with the applicable filters. This allows sales representatives to move from the Dashboard summary to the detailed Deal records. Filters Available filters may include: Fiscal Year Pipeline or Deal property My Performance The My Performance section provides a quick overview of the sales representative's individual performance. The section can display KPIs such as: Deals Won Conversion Rate Activities Completed Average Deal Size Time Period Users can select the applicable reporting period, such as: This Month Previous Period Other configured periods Performance Comparison Where applicable, KPI cards display a comparison with the previous period. For example: Activities Completed: 13 ↑ vs last period This allows users to understand changes in their recent performance. Performance Basis Where supported, users can select the basis us",
