    "label": "Bulk Actions",
    "title": "Bulk Actions",
    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/bulk-actions",
    "description": "Learn how to perform actions on multiple Deal records simultaneously.",
    "body": "Bulk Actions The Bulk Actions feature in the Deals module allows users to perform operations on multiple Deal records simultaneously. This helps sales teams efficiently manage large numbers of opportunities without updating each deal individually. Accessing Bulk Actions 1. Navigate to the Deals module. 2. Select one or more Deals using the checkboxes beside each record. 3. Once records are selected, the Bulk Actions toolbar appears at the bottom of the page. 4. Choose the required action to apply to all selected Deals. Available Bulk Actions Merge Combine multiple duplicate Deal records into a single Deal record. This action helps maintain clean and accurate Deal data by eliminating duplicate opportunities. Use Cases Duplicate Deals created accidentally. Multiple records representing the same sales opportunity. Data cleanup and consolidation. Steps 1. Select the Deals to be merged. 2. Click Merge . 3. Review the Deal information. 4. Select the values to retain where conflicts exist. 5. Confirm the merge. Note Only Deals representing the same opportunity should be merged. Assign Owner Assign the selected Deals to another sales representative or team member. Use Cases Territory reassignment. Workload balancing. Team restructuring. Ownership transfer. Steps 1. Select one or more Deals. 2. Click Assign Owner . 3. Choose the desired user. 4. Confirm the assignment. Add Tags Apply Tags to multiple Deals simultaneously. Tags help categorize opportunities and improve filtering, reporting, and segmentation. Example Tags High Priority Enterprise Strategic Account Renewal Opportunity Steps 1. Select the required Deals. 2. Click Add Tags . 3. Select or enter the desired Tags. 4. Save the changes. Add to Sequence Enroll selected Deals into a predefined Sequence. Sequences help automate follow up actions such as emails, reminders, and tasks associated with Deal progression. Steps 1. Select the Deals. 2. Click Add to Sequence . 3. Select the desired Sequence. 4. Confirm enrollment. Archive Move selected Deals to the archive while preserving their historical information. Archived Deals remain available for reporting and auditing purposes but are removed from active Deal management views. Use Cases Inactive opportunities. Obsolete Deals. Historical sales records. Steps 1. Select the Deals. 2. Click Archive . 3. Confirm the action. Delete Permanently remove selected Deal records from the CRM. Important: Deleted records may not be recoverable depending on system configuration and permissions. Steps 1. Select the Deals. 2. Click Delete . 3. Review the confirmation message. 4. Confirm deletion. Export Export selected Deal records for reporting, analysis, or data sharing. Common Uses Pipeline analysis. Revenue forecasting. Management reporting. Data backup. Steps 1. Select the Deals. 2. Click Export . Add to Workflow Add selected Deals to an existing Workflow. Workflows automate business processes and actions related to Deal management. Examples Deal qualification workflow. Follow up workflow. Approval workflow. Customer onboarding workflow. Steps 1. Select the required Deals. 2. Click Add to Workflow . 3. Select the desired Workflow. 4. Confirm the action. Best Practices Review selected records before applying Bulk Actions. Use Tags and Filters to identify groups of Deals requiring the same action. Verify Workflow and Sequence assignments before applying them to large numbers of Deals. Exercise caution when using Merge and Delete , as these actions can significantly affect Deal data. Ensure that duplicate records are reviewed carefully before merging.",
