    "label": "Deal Details",
    "title": "Deal Details",
    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/deal-details",
    "description": "Learn about the Deal Details page and its features.",
    "body": "Deal Details The Deal Details page provides a centralized view of all information related to a specific Deal. It enables users to track Deal progress, manage activities, monitor Deal performance, collaborate with stakeholders, and take actions that help move opportunities through the sales pipeline. Users can access a Deal's complete history, communication records, tasks, meetings, score insights, and AI powered recommendations from a single location. Deal Information The left panel displays the key details associated with the Deal. Depending on your organization's configuration, the following information may be available: Deal Title Account (Organization) Contact Pipeline Stage Deal Value Currency Status Deal Owner Tags Deal Score Note The fields displayed in the Deal Details section may vary based on the Deal Form configuration defined by your CRM administrator. Deal Stage Management The Deal Stage section visually represents the current position of the Deal within the selected sales pipeline. Each stage represents a milestone in the sales process and helps users understand the progress of the opportunity. Viewing the Current Stage The currently active stage is highlighted within the pipeline progression bar. Examples of stages may include: Qualification Property Matched Site Visit Scheduled Site Visit Completed Negotiation/Review Closed Won Closed Lost In some pipelines, stages may also display probability percentages that indicate the likelihood of successfully closing the Deal. Note Available stages depend on the pipeline configuration defined by your CRM administrator. Moving a Deal to Another Stage As the opportunity progresses, users can update the Deal stage to reflect the latest status. Steps 1. Open the required Deal record. 2. Navigate to the Insights tab. 3. Click Move the Stage . 4. Select the desired stage from the available list. The Deal is automatically updated within the pipeline. Benefits Maintains accurate pipeline visibility. Improves sales forecasting. Enables stage based automation. Provides better reporting and analytics. Marking a Deal as Won When a Deal is successfully closed, users can mark it as Won . Steps 1. Open the Deal record. 2. Click Won . 3. Confirm the action if prompted. Once marked as Won : The Deal is considered successfully closed. Revenue reporting is updated accordingly. Won Deal metrics are reflected in reports and dashboards. Marking a Deal as Lost When an opportunity is no longer being pursued, users can mark it as Lost . Steps 1. Open the Deal record. 2. Click Lost . 3. Confirm the action if prompted. Once marked as Lost : The Deal is removed from active sales forecasting. Loss metrics become available for reporting and analysis.",
