    "label": "Deal Scoring",
    "title": "Deal Scoring",
    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/deal-score",
    "description": "Learn how Deal Scoring helps prioritize opportunities in the sales pipeline.",
    "body": "Deal Scoring The Deal Score provides a numerical indication of the overall health and quality of a Deal. It helps sales teams prioritize opportunities and focus on Deals that are more likely to close successfully. The score is calculated using a combination of: Business Rules configured by administrators (Rule Based Scoring). AI Analysis based on buyer behavior, engagement patterns, Deal activity, and other predictive signals. Administrators can configure the contribution of each scoring method by defining the percentage ratio between Business Rule Scoring and AI Scoring in the Deal Scoring settings. Example Scoring Configuration Business Rules: 60% AI Analysis: 40% In this configuration: 60% of the final score is derived from predefined Business Rules. 40% of the final score is derived from AI driven analysis. The system combines both components to generate a single Deal Score that reflects both organizational priorities and real world buyer behavior. Benefits of Deal Scoring Deal Scoring helps organizations: Prioritize high potential opportunities. Identify Deals requiring attention. Provide objective Deal health measurement. Combine business expertise with AI driven insights. Deal Score Trend The Deal Score Trend section provides a visual representation of how a Deal's score changes over time. It helps users understand whether the overall health of a Deal is improving, declining, or remaining stable throughout the sales cycle. Since the Deal Score is calculated using a combination of Business Rule Scoring and AI Scoring , the Score Trend reflects the combined impact of both scoring methods. Purpose of the Score Trend The Score Trend enables users to: Monitor Deal health over time. Track the effectiveness of sales activities. Identify positive or negative engagement patterns. Detect potential Deal risks early. Measure the impact of buyer interactions and Deal progression. Understand how changes in scoring factors affect the overall Deal Score. Understanding the Score Trend Chart The chart displays historical changes in the Deal Score across a selected period. A Rising Trend Generally Indicates Increased buyer engagement. Positive Deal progression. Completion of important sales activities. Improved AI confidence in Deal success. Achievement of scoring criteria defined by Business Rules. A Declining Trend May Indicate Reduced customer engagement. Missed follow ups or activities. Stalled Deal progression. Negative engagement signals identified by AI. Changes in Rule Based Scoring conditions. A Stable Trend May Indicate Consistent engagement. No significant changes in Deal activity. Steady progression through the sales process. Factors That Influence Score Changes Score fluctuations can occur due to updates in either Business Rule Scoring or AI Scoring . Business Rule Factors Examples include: Deal moving to a new stage. Changes to Deal Value. Completion of required activities. Addition or removal of Tags. Updates to important Deal fields. Changes to administrator defined scoring rules. AI Factors Examples include: Buyer responsiveness. Email and meeting engagement. Activity frequency. Communication patterns. Historical conversion indicators. Changes in Deal momentum and risk signals. Because the final Deal Score combines both scoring methods, changes from either source may affect the trend. Viewing Historical Trends Users can analyze score performance across different time periods. Available options may include: Weekly (W) Monthly (M) Yearly (Y) All Time (All) These views help users identify short term score fluctuations as well as long term Deal performance patterns. Using Score Trends Effectively Sales teams can use the Score Trend to: Identify Deals gaining momentum. Detect opportunities requiring immediate attention. Validate the effectiveness of sales activities. Prioritize high potential opportunities. Support forecasting and pipeline reviews. Monitor the impact of Smart Nudge recommendations and follow up actions. Best P",
