    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/emails",
    "description": "Learn how to send and manage emails associated with Deals.",
    "body": "Emails Management The Emails feature allows users to compose, send, schedule, and track emails directly from the Deals module. All email communications are automatically associated with the corresponding Deal, providing a centralized view of customer interactions throughout the sales process. This eliminates the need to switch between external email applications and the CRM while ensuring complete communication history is maintained. Accessing Emails 1. Navigate to the Deals module. 2. Open the required Deal record. 3. Go to the Emails tab under the Activities section. 4. Click Compose Email . This opens the Email Composer . Email Composer The Email Composer allows users to create professional emails using rich formatting tools. Users can: Enter recipients. Add a subject. Compose the email body. Format text. Attach files. Insert templates. Schedule emails. Save drafts. Email Templates Users can insert predefined email templates to simplify communication and maintain consistency. Templates help users: Save time. Standardize communication. Reduce repetitive typing. Improve customer engagement. Insert Options The Email Composer supports inserting: Email Templates CRM Documents Meeting Links Quotes These items can be added directly into the email body. Attachments Users can attach supporting files while composing an email. Examples include: Proposal Documents Quotations Product Brochures Images PDFs Other supporting documents Send Options Users can choose one of the following options: Option Description Send Now Sends the email immediately. Schedule Send Schedules the email for a future date and time. Save Draft Saves the email for future editing. Schedule Send The Schedule Send option allows users to specify the exact date and time when an email should be delivered. Scheduled emails remain in the CRM until the configured delivery time. Save Draft If an email is not ready to be sent, users can save it as a draft. Draft emails can be edited and sent later. Email Status The CRM tracks the status of each email. Common statuses include: Draft Scheduled Sent Delivered Failed These statuses help users monitor email communication with customers. Email Activity Timeline All emails sent from the Deals module are automatically recorded in the Deal Activity Timeline . Each email entry displays information such as: Subject Sender Recipients Date and Time Delivery Status This provides complete visibility into communication history for the Deal. Best Practices Use email templates for consistent communication. Review recipients before sending emails. Attach relevant documents when required. Schedule follow up emails for important opportunities. Monitor email statuses to ensure successful delivery. Maintain complete communication history within the Deal record.",
