    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/meetings",
    "description": "Learn how to schedule and manage meetings associated with Deals.",
    "body": "Meetings Management The Meetings feature enables users to schedule, manage, and track meetings related to Deals directly within the CRM. It helps sales teams collaborate with customers, record important discussions, and maintain a complete history of interactions throughout the sales process. Meetings can also be synchronized with supported calendar providers, ensuring schedules remain up to date across integrated platforms. Accessing Meetings 1. Navigate to the Deals module. 2. Open the required Deal record. 3. Go to the Meetings tab under the Activities section. 4. Click Add . This opens the Meeting Scheduling form. Scheduling a Meeting Users can schedule meetings by providing the required information. Meeting Details Field Description Event Title Specifies the title of the meeting. From Displays the meeting organizer. Attendees Select internal users or external attendees. Start Date & Time Specifies when the meeting begins. End Date & Time Specifies when the meeting ends. Location Select the meeting location or virtual meeting provider. Description Add the meeting agenda or discussion points. Meeting Location Users can schedule meetings using supported meeting platforms such as: Google Meet Microsoft Teams Microsoft Outlook In Person If an online meeting provider is selected, the meeting link is automatically generated and shared with attendees. Attendees The Deal's primary contact is automatically added as an attendee. Users can also: Add internal CRM users. Invite external participants using their email addresses. Description The Description field allows users to record: Meeting agenda Discussion topics Preparation notes Follow up items Providing detailed descriptions helps participants prepare before the meeting. Saving the Meeting After entering the required details: 1. Review the meeting information. 2. Click Save . The meeting is: Added to the Deal Activity Timeline. Synchronized with the connected calendar. Shared with all invited attendees. Rescheduling Meetings Users can modify scheduled meetings whenever required. The following details can be updated: Date Time Attendees Meeting Location Description Changes are automatically synchronized with the connected calendar. Logging Meetings The Log Meeting feature allows users to manually record meetings that have already taken place. Logging meetings helps maintain an accurate interaction history and supports future reporting and collaboration. Log Meeting Details Users can record information such as: Field Description Meeting Title Title of the meeting Meeting Type Virtual, In Person, or Phone Date & Time Date and time when the meeting occurred Participants Internal and external attendees Summary Summary of the discussion Outcome Result of the meeting Follow up Task Create a follow up task if required Attachments Upload supporting documents Meeting Outcomes Users can record outcomes such as: Successful Follow up Required Rescheduled No Response No Show Cancelled Recording outcomes helps track customer engagement and determine the next course of action. Attachments Supporting documents can be uploaded while logging a meeting. Examples include: Presentation files Proposal documents Meeting notes Images Other supporting files Saving a Logged Meeting After entering all required information: 1. Review the meeting details. 2. Click Submit . The meeting is successfully logged and added to the Deal Activity Timeline.",
