    "body": "Notes Management The Notes feature allows users to capture important information, discussions, observations, and follow up details related to a Deal. Notes help sales teams maintain a complete history of customer interactions, making it easier for team members to understand the context of an opportunity and collaborate effectively. Accessing Notes 1. Navigate to the Deals module. 2. Open the required Deal record. 3. Go to the Notes tab under the Activities section. 4. Click Add Note . This opens the Note Editor . Creating a Note After opening the Note Editor: 1. Enter the required note content. 2. Format the text if required. 3. Click Submit . The note is saved and displayed in the Deal timeline. Note Editor Features The Note Editor provides rich text editing capabilities, allowing users to: Enter formatted text. Create bullet and numbered lists. Insert hyperlinks. Add images. Create tables. Highlight important information. Managing Notes Users can perform the following actions on existing notes: View notes. Edit notes. Delete notes. Search notes. Pin important notes. Viewing Notes All notes are displayed in chronological order under the Notes section of the Deal. Each note displays: Author Date and Time Note Content This provides complete visibility into discussions and updates throughout the Deal lifecycle. Best Practices Record customer discussions immediately after meetings or calls. Keep notes clear and concise. Include important decisions and action items. Update notes whenever new information becomes available. Use notes to maintain a complete history of customer interactions.",
