    "description": "Learn how to create, upload, manage, and track quotes associated with Deals.",
    "body": "Quotes Management The Quotes functionality in the Deals Module helps sales teams create, upload, manage, send, and track customer facing quotation documents directly within a Deal. Quotes help organizations maintain pricing transparency, standardize commercial communication, and centralize quotation management throughout the Deal lifecycle. What is a Quote? A Quote is a commercial pricing document shared with customers containing: Product or service pricing Quantity Taxes Discounts Commercial terms Validity period Quotes are mainly used during pricing discussions and negotiations. Importance of Quotes Quotes help organizations: Share accurate pricing. Improve pricing transparency. Maintain quotation history. Reduce pricing errors. Track customer approvals. Accessing Quotes Quotes can be accessed from the Deal Details page under the Quotes tab. Creating a Quote Step 1: Open Quotes Tab Navigate to the Deals module. Open the required Deal. Go to the Quotes tab. Step 2: Click Add Click the Add button. This opens the Quote Creation Options window. Quote Creation Options The CRM provides multiple methods for quote management. Option 1: Upload Quote This option allows users to upload an already created quotation document. Steps 1. Click Upload Quote . 2. Upload the quotation document. 3. Add the required details. 4. Save the quote. Upload Quote Features Users can: Upload quotation files. Associate quotes with Deals. Track uploaded quotations. Maintain centralized quotation history. Supported File Formats The CRM supports: PDF DOC DOCX Note The maximum file size may vary depending on your organization's configuration. Option 2: Upload & Send via CXAstra This option allows users to upload and directly send quotations using CRM communication channels. Features Direct customer sharing. Email tracking. Customer engagement monitoring. Centralized communication management. Option 3: Create Quote (Quick) This option allows users to quickly generate quotations directly within the CRM. Steps 1. Click Create Quote . 2. Add products or services. 3. Enter quantity and pricing. 4. Apply taxes and discounts. 5. Save the quote. Quote Validations The CRM validates the following before a quote is created or shared: Quote currency must match the Deal currency. Discounts must follow organization policies. Validity date is mandatory. Discount Approval Rules If discounts exceed the permitted limits, the CRM may require manager approval before the quote can be approved or shared with the customer. Quote Lifecycle Quotes generally move through the following stages: Status Description Draft Quote created. Pending Approval Waiting for approval. Approved Approved for customer sharing. Sent Shared with the customer. Accepted Customer accepted the quote. Rejected Customer rejected the quote. Expired Quote validity expired. Quote Tracking The CRM tracks quotation activities throughout the Deal lifecycle. This includes: Quote uploads. Quote sharing history. Status updates. Customer responses. Activity timeline records. Activity Timeline Integration All quote activities are automatically recorded in the Deal Activity Timeline . This includes: Uploads. Status changes. Sharing activities. Approval updates. Customer interactions. This provides complete visibility into the quotation lifecycle directly from the Deal record. AI and Smart Insights Sales Astra CRM analyzes quotation activities to provide valuable insights, including: Deal Scoring. Engagement Insights. Smart Nudges. Follow up Recommendations. Customer interactions with quotations help the CRM identify buying intent, measure customer engagement, and recommend appropriate next actions. Best Practices Verify pricing before sharing quotations. Ensure discounts comply with organizational policies. Keep quotation statuses updated throughout the sales process. Review customer responses regularly. Monitor quotation validity dates to avoid sending expired quotes. Use Activity Timeline and Smart Nudges to track engag",
