    "label": "Search and Filters",
    "title": "Search and Filters",
    "to": "/docs/Deals-Module/search-and-filters",
    "description": "Learn how to search and filter Deal records in the Deals module.",
    "body": "Search and Filters Deal Filters and Advanced Filters The Deals Module provides filtering options that help users quickly organize and locate Deal records based on specific conditions. Filters improve Deal visibility and help sales teams efficiently manage opportunities within the sales pipeline. Default Deal Filters The Deals Module provides quick filters such as: Deal Owner Deal Status Close Date Create Date These filters are displayed at the top of the Deals List View for quick access. Deal Owner Filter The Deal Owner filter allows users to view Deals assigned to specific users. Deal Status Filter The Deal Status filter helps users organize Deals based on their current status. Common Statuses Open Won Lost This helps users quickly identify active or closed opportunities. Close Date Filter The Close Date filter allows users to filter Deals based on expected closure timelines. This helps teams prioritize Deals nearing closure. Created Date Filter The Created Date filter helps users identify Deals created during a specific time period. Advanced Filters The Deals Module also provides an Advanced Filter option for applying multiple filter conditions simultaneously. This helps users create highly specific Deal searches. Search Deals The Search Deals feature allows users to quickly locate specific Deal records by searching within selected Deal fields. This helps users find opportunities faster, especially when working with large numbers of Deal records. Accessing Deal Search 1. Navigate to the Deals module. 2. Locate the Search box above the Deal list. 3. Click the Field Selection dropdown next to the Search bar. 4. Select one or more fields to search within. 5. Enter the search value in the Search box. The system displays matching Deal records based on the selected search criteria. Selecting Search Fields Users can choose the fields that should be included in the search. Common Searchable Fields Include Deal Title Status Deal Value Deal Score Pipeline Stage Close Date Created Date Contact Note The available search fields may vary depending on your CRM configuration and the columns available in the Deals module. Searching for Deals After selecting the required search field(s), enter the value you want to find. Example 1: Search by Deal Title 1. Select Deal Title from the field selector. 2. Enter \"CRM Implementation\" in the Search box. 3. The system displays Deals whose titles match the entered value. Example 2: Search by Pipeline 1. Select Pipeline . 2. Enter \"Enterprise Pipeline\" . 3. The system displays Deals associated with that pipeline. Best Practices Select only the fields relevant to your search to improve search accuracy. Use Deal Title when searching for a specific opportunity. Use Pipeline or Stage when searching for groups of Deals in a particular sales process. Combine search with filters and Custom Views to quickly narrow down results.",
