    "body": "Deal Activities Management The Deals module supports comprehensive activity management to help sales teams track all customer interactions and next steps directly within the Deal lifecycle. Activities help maintain a centralized history of communication, collaboration, follow ups, and engagement related to a Deal. Purpose of Deal Activities Deal Activities help organizations: Track all customer touchpoints. Maintain communication history. Improve collaboration. Monitor follow ups. Increase visibility into Deal progress. Improve customer engagement management. Deal Activities Timeline All activities are displayed inside the Deal Details page under the Activities section. Activities appear in a chronological timeline for easy tracking and visibility. Activity Filters Users can filter activities by: Meetings Emails Tasks Notes This helps users quickly locate specific interactions. Tasks Management Tasks help sales teams manage action items and follow ups related to Deals. Users can: Create Tasks Assign Tasks Set reminders Track completion status Step 1: Open the Deal Record Navigate to the Deals Module. Open the required Deal record. Go to the Tasks tab inside the Activities section. Step 2: Create a New Task Click Create Task . This opens the Task Creation form. Task Statuses Common statuses include: Open In Progress Completed Overdue Task Validations The following validations are applied while creating a task: Title is required. Title length must be between 3–100 characters . Due date must be today or a future date . Priority defaults to Medium if not selected. Task Notifications The CRM sends the following notifications: Due date reminders. Assignment notifications. Follow up alerts. Notifications are delivered through in app notifications or email. Step 3: Save the Task After entering the required details: Click the Save button. The task will be created and linked to the selected Deal.",
