    "description": "Configure Your CRM Before your team begins using CX Astra CRM, it is recommended to complete the essential organization and system configuration. These settings establish your",
    "body": "Configure Your CRM Before your team begins using CX Astra CRM, it is recommended to complete the essential organization and system configuration. These settings establish your organization's identity, user access, operational preferences, and communication platform configuration. This guide provides an overview of the recommended setup sequence. Each section links to its dedicated documentation for detailed configuration instructions. Recommended Setup Sequence Complete the following setup tasks in the recommended order: 1. Organization Settings 2. User Management 3. Roles 4. Configure CRM Settings 5. Pulse Settings 1. Organization Settings Navigate to: Organization Settings allow administrators to configure and manage organization wide settings within CX Astra CRM. These settings establish: Company identity Operational preferences Branding standards Regional configurations Work schedules Organization Settings help ensure consistency across: Billing and invoicing CRM communications Workflows and automations Reporting and dashboards SLA calculations User facing branding The Organization Settings module consists of the following sections: Profile Localization Work Schedule Branding 👉 Learn more about Organization Settings → 2. User Management Navigate to: The User Management module allows administrators to manage user access across the organization. Administrators can: Invite users Assign workspaces Manage user status Activate or deactivate users Resend or cancel invitations Delete users Search and filter users User Management capabilities include: Role reassignment Workspace assignment Invitation management User activation control Access deactivation Soft deletion handling 👉 Learn more about User Management → Related guides: Manage Users Access and Sharing 3. Roles Navigate to: Roles define how users access and interact with CX Astra CRM. Roles determine: Which modules a user can access What actions a user can perform What records a user can view or manage Assignment capabilities AI and Pulse access permissions Administrative privileges The Roles module supports: System Roles Custom Roles Administrators can configure: Module Level Access Action Level Permissions Visibility Scope Logic Assignment Scope Logic 👉 Learn more about Roles and Permissions → 4. Configure CRM Settings After configuring users and roles, administrators can customize CRM behavior from the Configure section. Available configuration areas include: Leads Configure Lead Scoring to define how Lead Scores are calculated using: Manual Scoring AI Scoring Blended Scoring 👉 Learn more about Lead Scoring → Deals Configure Deal Pipelines, Deal Settings, Deal Scoring, and Deal Import to define your organization's sales process. Administrators can: Create pipelines Configure stages Define stage order Set stage probabilities Configure stage behaviors Deal Settings allow administrators to configure: Sales Model Buyer Type Behavior Deal Origin Related configuration: Pipeline Deal Settings Deal Scoring Deal Import Custom Fields Tags 5. Pulse Settings Pulse Settings allow administrators to configure how the customer engagement platform operates. The Pulse Settings module consists of: Channels Users & Access Assignment Rules Knowledge Base Support Availability Global Settings These settings help organizations: Deliver consistent customer support experiences Automate responses to common queries Route conversations to the appropriate agents Manage support team access Define business availability Maintain a centralized knowledge repository Configure chatbot behavior across channels 👉 Learn more about Pulse Settings → Setup Checklist Before using CX Astra CRM, verify that the following configuration has been completed: ✅ Organization Settings configured ✅ Users added and managed ✅ Roles and permissions configured ✅ CRM configuration completed ✅ Pulse configured (if applicable) Once these steps are completed, your CX Astra CRM workspace is ready for day to day operations.",
