    "description": "Learn how to create and manage lead records in CX Astra CRM.",
    "body": "Overview The Leads module enables users to capture and manage potential customers within CX Astra CRM. Creating accurate lead records helps sales teams organize prospects, track interactions, and streamline the sales process. The Lead Creation form is fully configurable by CRM administrators. Depending on your organization's configuration, the form may include different sections, custom fields, validation rules, and business specific information. Purpose Creating lead records allows your organization to: Capture enquiries from potential customers. Organize prospect information in a centralized location. Assign ownership to sales representatives. Track lead qualification throughout the sales cycle. Prepare leads for conversion into deals. Accessing the Lead Creation Form To create a new Lead: 1. Log in to CX Astra CRM . 2. Navigate to Leads from the left navigation menu. 3. Click Create Lead . The Lead Creation form opens. :::note The Lead Creation form shown above is the default form, containing the standard fields provided by the system. You can customize the form by adding, removing, or modifying fields through Custom Fields to align with your organization's specific requirements and lead capture process. ::: Section Description Basic Information Captures the Lead's name and general details. Contact Information Stores email address, phone number, and communication details. Company Information Records company related information. Lead Management Defines Lead Owner, Status, Source, and other business fields. Address Details Stores location and address information. Social Information Stores social media profiles and website details. Field Requirements While entering Lead information, keep the following in mind: Mandatory fields are marked with an asterisk ( \\ ). Validation rules are enforced automatically. Dropdowns display administrator configured values. Lookup fields allow linking existing CRM records. Custom fields may appear depending on your organization's configuration. :::tip Complete as much information as possible while creating a Lead to improve qualification accuracy and future reporting. ::: Save the Lead After entering the required information: 1. Review all entered details. 2. Click Create Lead . If all validations are successful: The Lead is created successfully. A confirmation message is displayed. The Lead becomes available in the Leads list. Example A sales representative receives an enquiry from a customer through the company website. The representative creates a Lead with the following information: Field Value Lead Name John Smith Company ABC Technologies Email john.smith@example.com Phone +1 9876543210 Lead Source Website Lead Owner Sarah Johnson Status New After saving, the Lead becomes available for qualification and follow up. Best Practices Complete all available Lead information whenever possible. Assign the correct Lead Owner during creation. Apply Tags for easier segmentation. Verify contact details before saving. Use meaningful Lead Sources for accurate reporting. Avoid creating duplicate Lead records.",
