    "label": "Custom Views",
    "title": "Custom Views",
    "to": "/docs/Leads-Module/custom-views",
    "description": "The Leads Module in Sales Astra CRM allows users to create and manage custom views based on filters, columns, and sorting preferences. Custom views help Sales Executives and Sales",
    "body": "The Leads Module in Sales Astra CRM allows users to create and manage custom views based on filters, columns, and sorting preferences. Custom views help Sales Executives and Sales Managers quickly switch between different working styles and focus on the most relevant lead data. Examples of custom views include: Hot Leads My Leads This Week High Score Leads Uncontacted Leads Recently Created Leads By using custom views, users can improve productivity, organize their pipeline efficiently, and reduce repetitive filtering activities. Purpose of Custom Views Custom views help users: Save frequently used filter combinations Customize visible columns Sort lead data based on business needs Access important leads quickly Improve daily workflow efficiency Personalize lead management experience Each custom view is user specific and applies only to the logged in user. Features Available in Custom Views Users can configure the following while creating a custom view: Columns to Display Users can choose which columns should appear in the lead table. Example Columns Lead Name Score Source Owner Status Company Preferred Channel Last Activity Date Created Date Next Stage This allows users to focus only on the most relevant information. Saved Filters Users can apply and save filters while creating a custom view. Example Filters Score 80 Created in Last 7 Days Status = Qualified Assigned To = Current User Source = Website These saved filters help users quickly access specific lead groups. Sort Order Configuration Users can define sorting preferences for the custom view. Example Sorting Options Score Descending Created Date Ascending Last Activity Date Descending Company Name Alphabetically Sorting helps users organize lead data efficiently. Creating a Custom View Step 1: Navigate to Leads Module Login to Sales Astra CRM. Open the Leads Module from the sidebar. Step 2: Open Create View Popup Click on the Add View option. The Create New View popup window will appear. In the View Name field: Enter a unique name for the custom view. Example View Names Hot Leads My Leads This Week Enterprise Opportunities High Priority Leads Step 3: Configure Filters Under the Where section: Select a filter field. Choose a condition. Enter the filter value. Example Filter Condition Value Score Greater Than 80 Status Equals Qualified Created Date Preset Last 7 Days Step 4: Save the View After completing the configuration: Click on the Create View button. The custom view will now be saved successfully. Default View The system always provides a: Default View Important Notes The Default View cannot be deleted. It acts as the standard lead listing view. Users can always return to the default configuration. Editing Custom Views Users can modify previously saved custom views. Editable Configurations Filters Columns Sorting View Name After updating the configuration, users can save the changes. Deleting Custom Views Users can delete custom views that are no longer required. Important Notes Only user created views can be deleted. The Default View cannot be removed. User Specific Configuration Custom views are private to the logged in user. Behavior Changes are not shared globally. Other users cannot see personal custom views. Each user can maintain their own working style independently. This ensures personalized pipeline management for every user. Benefits of Custom Views Custom views provide several advantages: Faster access to important leads Reduced repetitive filtering Improved productivity Better lead organization Personalized workflow management Improved sales efficiency",
