    "body": "Lead to Deal Conversion The CRM system supports Lead to Deal Conversion , allowing qualified leads to be converted into active business opportunities. This functionality helps sales teams move potential customers from the lead management stage into the sales pipeline for further opportunity tracking and revenue management. What is Lead to Deal Conversion? Lead to Deal Conversion is the process of converting a qualified lead into a deal once the lead shows strong business potential or buying intent. After conversion: The lead becomes an active sales opportunity. A deal record is created. The opportunity enters the sales pipeline. Sales teams can start negotiation and deal management activities. When Does Lead Conversion Happen? A lead can be converted into a deal in two ways: Automatic Conversion: Triggered when lead status changes to Qualified . Manual Conversion: Triggered using the Convert to Deal button. Automatic Lead to Deal Conversion When a lead status is updated to Qualified , the CRM automatically opens the Deal Creation form. This helps sales users immediately create a business opportunity without manually navigating to the Deals Module. Step 1: Open Lead Record Navigate to the Leads Module. Open the required lead record. Step 2: Change Lead Status Update the lead status to Qualified . Step 3: Deal Creation Form Appears Once the lead is marked as Qualified : The Deal Creation popup automatically appears. Lead information is pre filled into the deal form. Manual Lead to Deal Conversion Users can also manually convert a lead into a deal from the Lead Details page. Manual Conversion Process Step 1: Open Lead Details Page Navigate to the Leads Module. Open the required lead record. Step 2: Click Convert to Deal Click the Convert to Deal button. A confirmation pop up appears asking whether you want to update the lead status to Qualified. Click Yes to proceed. The Deal Creation form opens, allowing you to create a new deal from the qualified lead. Pre Filled Information The system may automatically populate fields such as: Field Auto Filled from Lead Deal Title Lead Name Contact Lead Contact Account Associated Organization Deal Owner Current Lead Owner Pipeline Default Sales Pipeline Stage Qualification Status Open Deal Fields During Conversion Users can update or enter additional information such as: Buyer Type Deal Value Close Date Tags Currency Pipeline Stage before creating the deal. Relationship Between Lead and Deal After conversion: The deal remains linked to the original lead. Activity history is preserved. Customer interactions remain traceable. This helps maintain a complete sales history throughout the lifecycle. Benefits of Lead to Deal Conversion Lead conversion helps organizations: Move qualified leads into the sales pipeline quickly. Reduce manual data entry. Improve sales workflow efficiency. Maintain relationship continuity. Improve opportunity tracking. Increase conversion visibility.",
