    "body": "Creating and Managing Meetings The Meetings feature allows CRM users to schedule and manage meetings with leads directly from the CRM system. Meetings can be synchronized with external calendar providers such as: Google Calendar Microsoft Outlook Microsoft Exchange This helps users track meetings inside the CRM while keeping their external calendars updated automatically. Meetings Tab The Lead Details page contains a: Meetings tab under the Activities section. Users can: Create meetings Log manual meetings View scheduled meetings Reschedule meetings Delete meetings Available Meeting Options The Meetings section provides the following actions: Create Meeting Log Meeting Creating a Meeting Step 1: Open the Lead Record Navigate to the Leads Module. Open the required lead record. Go to the Meetings tab. Step 2: Click Create Meeting Click the Add button. This opens the Meeting Scheduling flow. Scheduling a Meeting After calendar connection is completed, users can schedule meetings. Meeting Fields Field Description Event Title Title of the meeting From User scheduling the meeting Attendees Lead email and additional attendees Start Date & Time Meeting start date and time End Date & Time Meeting end date and time Location Google Meet, Outlook Meet, or In Person Description Meeting agenda or notes Attendees The lead email is automatically added as an attendee. Users can also: Add multiple users Add additional email addresses Calendar Slot Selection Users can select meeting slots using the calendar view. If existing events are already scheduled, they will be displayed to help avoid scheduling conflicts. Meeting Location Options Users can select meeting locations such as: Google Meet Outlook Meet In Person Online meeting links are automatically generated for supported providers. This information is shared with all meeting attendees. Description Field Users can enter: Meeting agenda Discussion topics Notes Follow up details Saving the Meeting After entering the required details: Click Save . The meeting will: Sync to the connected calendar. Be added to the CRM activity timeline. Notify attendees. Rescheduling Meetings Users can update: Meeting date Time slot Attendees Updated information automatically syncs with the connected calendar. Logging Meetings The Log Meeting feature allows users to manually record meetings that have already taken place with a lead. This helps maintain accurate activity history, improves team visibility, and supports reporting and analytics within the CRM system. Logged meetings are automatically added to: Lead Activity Timeline Meetings List View Accessing Log Meeting Steps to Open Log Meeting Navigate to the Leads Module. Open the required lead record. Go to the Meetings tab under Activities. Click Log Meeting . This opens the Log Meeting form in a modal or side panel. Log Meeting Form Fields The form captures structured meeting information for better tracking and reporting. Field Description Meeting Title Enter the title of the meeting Meeting Type Select meeting type Date & Time of Meeting Select the meeting date and time Participants Add internal users and external participants Summary Enter meeting discussion details Outcome Select the meeting outcome Follow up Task Create a follow up task if required File Attachment Upload supporting files or documents Meeting Type Options Users can select meeting types such as: Virtual In Person Phone Virtual Meeting Providers If the meeting type is selected as: Virtual users can choose providers such as: Microsoft Teams Google Meet Zoom Meeting Date and Time Selection Users must select: Meeting date Meeting time using the Date Time Picker . Participants Users can add: Internal CRM users External participant email addresses This helps maintain complete attendee records for the meeting. Meeting Outcome Users can select meeting outcomes such as: Successful Follow up Required No Response No Show Up Rescheduled Cancelled This helps track meeting effectiveness and follow up re",
