    "to": "/docs/Leads-Module/search-and-filters",
    "description": "The Leads Module in Sales Astra CRM provides powerful search and filtering capabilities that help users quickly locate and manage lead records efficiently. These features allow",
    "body": "The Leads Module in Sales Astra CRM provides powerful search and filtering capabilities that help users quickly locate and manage lead records efficiently. These features allow Sales Executives and Sales Managers to search for leads using specific columns, apply filters, and narrow down lead data based on business requirements. Search Functionality The Leads Module includes a search bar that allows users to search for lead records dynamically. Users can search for specific data by selecting a column and entering matching values. Features of Search Functionality Column Based Search Users can select a specific column from the dropdown and search only within that column. Example Search Columns Lead Name Email Contact Number Company Name Lead Owner Lead Status Source How Search Works Step by Step Process Step 1: Open Leads Module Navigate to the Leads Module from the sidebar menu. Step 2: Use the Search Bar At the top of the lead listing page, users will find: Search input field Select Column dropdown Step 3: Select a Column Click the: Select Column dropdown and choose the column in which the search should be performed. Example Lead Name Email Company Phone Number Step 4: Enter Search Value Type the value to search inside the selected column. Example: If the search column is Status , the search value can be Qualified . Benefits of Column Based Search Column based searching helps users: Find records faster Reduce manual searching Improve lead tracking Quickly access customer information Improve operational efficiency Filter Functionality The Leads Module also provides advanced filtering functionality for refining lead records. Filters help users display only relevant leads based on selected conditions. Available Filters Users can filter lead data using multiple filter categories. Lead Owner Filter Allows users to filter leads assigned to specific sales representatives. Lead Status Filter Users can filter leads based on status. Example status filters include: New, Contacted, Negotiation, and Qualified. Example Statuses New Contacted Negotiation Qualified Created Date Filter Users can filter leads based on creation date. Available Options Today Yesterday Last 7 Days Last 30 Days This Month This Year Custom Range Last Activity Filter Filters leads based on the most recent activity performed. Example Recently Contacted Leads No Activity Leads Last Follow Up This Week Advanced Filters The system also supports Advanced Filters for creating complex filtering conditions. Users can combine multiple filters together for more refined lead management. Available Filter Fields Users can filter leads using fields such as: Lead Status Source Lead Owner Score Created Date Last Activity Date Preferred Channel Company Assigned To The available filter options are dynamically loaded from the backend. Supported Conditions Depending on the selected field type, users can apply conditions such as: Equals Not Equals Contains Greater Than Less Than Between Is Empty Is Not Empty",
