    "label": "Navigation Guide",
    "title": "Navigation Guide",
    "to": "/docs/navigation",
    "description": "Navigation Guide The CX Astra CRM interface is designed to provide quick access to customer information, sales activities, communication channels, and administrative settings from",
    "body": "Navigation Guide The CX Astra CRM interface is designed to provide quick access to customer information, sales activities, communication channels, and administrative settings from a single workspace. This guide introduces the primary navigation areas of the application and explains how users can efficiently move between different sections of the CRM. CRM Navigation Overview The CX Astra CRM interface consists of the following navigation areas: Left Navigation Sidebar Top Navigation Bar Each section is designed to help users quickly access CRM features without leaving the current workspace. Left Navigation Sidebar The left navigation sidebar provides access to the core CRM modules. From here, users can navigate to: Dashboard Leads Deals Contacts Organizations Activities Calendar Pulse AI Assistant Content Each module opens its own workspace while keeping the navigation consistent throughout the application. Dashboard The Dashboard provides a high level overview of your CRM. From the Dashboard, users can monitor: Sales performance Assigned work Recent activities Business insights Key metrics Module Navigation Selecting any module from the sidebar opens its dedicated workspace. Each module contains its own pages and features. For example, opening the Contacts module displays pages such as: Overview Creating Contacts Bulk Actions Search & Filters Contact Activities Linked Deals Linked Leads Similarly, every CRM module contains its own navigation structure based on the available functionality. Top Navigation Bar The top navigation bar provides quick access to global CRM features that are available from anywhere in the application. These include: Global Search Create AI Assistant Pulse Inbox Notifications Settings User Profile Unlike the left navigation, these features remain accessible regardless of the currently selected module. Global Search The Global Search allows users to quickly locate CRM information without manually browsing through modules. Users can search for: Leads Deals Contacts Organizations Activities Search results help users navigate directly to the required record. Create Menu The Create button provides quick access to creating new CRM records. Depending on user permissions, users can create records such as: Lead Deal Contact Organization This enables users to add new records from anywhere within the CRM. Astra ai Astra ai provides users with instant guidance while working inside the CRM. Users can ask questions related to: CRM features Module functionality Product usage Configuration guidance General CRM workflows Astra ai helps users resolve questions without leaving the application. Pulse Inbox The Pulse Inbox icon provides quick access to customer conversations managed through the Pulse communication module. Selecting this icon opens the Pulse Inbox for managing conversations. Notifications The Notifications section displays important updates across the CRM. Examples include: Record assignments Activity reminders Meeting notifications Workflow updates System notifications Unread notifications are indicated by a notification badge. Settings The Settings module allows administrators to configure organization wide CRM settings. Configuration areas include: Organization Settings User Management Roles Teams Access Control Branding Localization Work Schedule Custom Fields Automation Integrations The available settings depend on the user's role and permissions. User Profile Menu The User Profile menu provides access to personal account options. Available options include: Profile Work Status Switch Workspace Logout Users can update their work availability, switch between accessible workspaces, or manage their personal profile from this menu. Navigating Between Modules Users can switch between CRM modules at any time by selecting a module from the left navigation sidebar. The current module remains highlighted, making it easy to identify the active workspace. Moving between modules does not require returning to the Das",
