    "body": "Organization Settings Overview The Organization Settings allow administrators to configure and manage organization wide settings within SalesAstra. These settings establish the company identity, operational preferences, branding standards, regional configurations, and work schedules used across the platform. Organization Settings ensure consistency across: Billing and invoicing CRM communications Workflows and automations Reporting and dashboards SLA calculations User facing branding :::note Only users with Admin or authorized permissions can access and modify these settings. ::: Accessing Organization Settings Navigate to: Settings → Organization Settings The Organization Settings module contains the following sections: Profile Localization Work Schedule Branding Target Management 1. Organization Profile The Organization Profile section stores the company’s core business information and primary contact details. Purpose This information is used across multiple modules including: Billing and invoices CRM generated emails Legal and compliance references Reports and exports Organization identity display Company Details Company Name This name is used throughout the CRM for organizational identity. Legal Company Name Optional field used for: Invoices Contracts Compliance documents Legal references Industry Administrators can select from predefined industries. Examples Information Technology Healthcare Manufacturing Education Company Size Select the employee range that best represents the organization. Examples 1–10 11–50 51–200 201–500 500+ Website URL Enter the organization's official website address. Address Configuration Registered Address Store the official business address. Fields Include Address Line 1 Address Line 2 City State Country ZIP / Postal Code Billing Address Administrators can choose: Same as Registered Address Separate Billing Address :::note If Separate Billing Address is selected, additional address fields become available. ::: Primary Contact (POC) Details The Primary Point of Contact (POC) represents the organization's main business contact. The POC information is used for: Administrative communications Billing related notifications Account management interactions Customer success and support communications",
