    "to": "/docs/Organizations-Module/linked-deals",
    "description": "Learn how to view and manage Deals associated with an Organization.",
    "body": "Linked Deals The Linked Deals tab provides a centralized view of all Deals associated with an Organization. It enables users to monitor every sales opportunity related to a business account without navigating to the Deals module. This helps sales teams understand the complete sales pipeline for an Organization, monitor deal progress, and track revenue opportunities from a single location. Overview An Organization can have multiple Deals representing different business opportunities, projects, renewals, or sales engagements. The Linked Deals tab serves as a central location for viewing and managing these opportunities throughout the sales lifecycle. All Deals associated with the selected Organization are displayed, providing complete visibility into the account's revenue pipeline. Viewing Linked Deals To view linked Deals: 1. Navigate to the Organizations module. 2. Open the required Organization record. 3. Select the Linked Deals tab. The system displays all Deals associated with the Organization. Deal Summary The Linked Deals page provides a summary of the Organization's sales opportunities. The summary includes: Total Linked Deals – Total number of Deals associated with the Organization. Open Deals – Number of active Deals currently in progress. Won Deals – Number of successfully closed Deals. Lost Deals – Number of Deals that were not converted. Total Pipeline Value – Combined value of all linked Deals. These metrics help users quickly evaluate the sales potential of the Organization. Deal Information Each linked Deal displays important information, including: Deal Name Pipeline Stage Deal Value Deal Owner Expected Close Date Probability Deal Status This information allows users to quickly review the progress and health of each sales opportunity. Opening a Deal Each Deal includes a View Deal option. Selecting View Deal opens the corresponding Deal Details page, where users can: View complete Deal information. Review Deal activities. Manage proposals and quotations. Track Deal progress. Monitor Deal scoring and smart nudges. Update the Deal stage. Creating a New Deal Users can create a new Deal directly from the Linked Deals tab. Steps 1. Open the required Organization. 2. Navigate to the Linked Deals tab. 3. Click Create Deal . 4. Enter the required Deal information. 5. Click Save . The newly created Deal is automatically associated with the selected Organization. Relationship Management Sales Astra CRM automatically maintains the relationship between Organizations and Deals. When a Deal is linked to an Organization: The Deal appears under the Organization's Linked Deals tab. The Organization is displayed in the Deal record. Changes to the Deal are reflected across the CRM. The relationship remains intact unless it is manually updated. This ensures accurate account level tracking throughout the sales lifecycle. Benefits The Linked Deals tab helps users: View all Deals associated with an Organization. Monitor the complete sales pipeline for an account. Track revenue opportunities from a single location. Create new Deals directly from the Organization page. Access Deal records without leaving the Organization module. Maintain complete visibility into account level sales activities.",
