    "description": "Learn how to manage customer conversations using Pulse Inbox.",
    "body": "Pulse Inbox Overview Pulse Inbox is a centralized workspace for managing customer conversations across multiple channels such as Pulse, WhatsApp, Instagram, and Messenger . It allows agents to view conversations, respond to customers, assign priorities, create leads, add internal notes, and manage conversation outcomes from a single screen. Pulse Inbox Layout The Pulse Inbox consists of three main sections. Conversation List Panel Located on the left side of the screen, this panel displays all customer conversations. Each conversation displays: Channel icon Customer name or identifier Priority Current status Assigned user initials (if assigned) Latest message preview Timestamp Users can switch between channels using: All Chat Pulse WhatsApp Instagram Messenger Conversation Thread Panel The center panel displays the complete conversation history. This section allows users to: View customer messages View agent responses Send replies Attach files Add internal notes Generate AI summaries Create leads End conversations Contact Information Panel The right panel displays customer and conversation details. Contact Information Contact Name Email Address Mobile Number Conversation Details Status Assigned Agent Channel First Message Date Priority AI Summary Displays a generated summary of the conversation when available. Searching and Filtering Conversations Pulse Inbox provides multiple options for locating conversations. Search Use the search bar to quickly find conversations. Users can search using: Customer name Mobile number Email address Conversation keywords Search results update dynamically as text is entered. Filters Conversations can be filtered using: Read Last Activity Tag Priority Assignee Additional filter options can be accessed using the Filters icon. Conversation Views Users can switch between: All Assigned Unassigned Not Responded Conversations can also be grouped by: New In Progress Completed All Managing Conversation Priority Each conversation can be assigned a priority level to indicate urgency. Priority levels include: High Medium Low #@# To update priority 1. Open the conversation. 2. Click the Priority selector in the conversation footer. 3. Select the required priority. The updated priority is displayed in both the conversation list and the conversation details. Internal Notes Internal notes allow agents to capture information related to a conversation for internal reference. Notes are visible only to internal users and are not shared with customers. Common Uses Recording follow up actions Capturing qualification details Sharing context with team members Storing important observations Creating a Lead When a conversation represents a potential sales opportunity, a lead can be created directly from Pulse Inbox . To create a lead 1. Open the conversation. 2. Click Create Lead . 3. Complete the required information. 4. Click Save . After successful creation: The conversation displays the Lead Created status. Lead information becomes available in the Contact Information panel. Users can access the lead record through View in CRM . AI Summary Pulse Inbox can generate an AI powered summary of a conversation. The summary helps users quickly understand: Customer intent Topics discussed Key information collected Suggested next steps To generate a summary, click Generate AI Summary . Marking a Conversation as Insufficient Data If a conversation does not contain enough information for further qualification or follow up, it can be marked as Insufficient Data . This option is available from: More Actions menu Quick Actions panel Marking a Conversation as Junk Conversations that are irrelevant, spam, or do not require further action can be marked as Junk . This option is available from: More Actions menu Quick Actions panel Ending a Conversation Agents can close a conversation when no further interaction is required. To end a conversation 1. Open the conversation. 2. Click End Conversation . The option is available from: Conver",
