    "label": "Widget Setup",
    "title": "Widget Setup",
    "to": "/docs/Pulse-Settings/Channels/Widget-Setup",
    "description": "Widget Setup The Widget Setup tab controls the appearance, behavior, branding, and installation of the website chat widget. These settings determine how visitors experience the",
    "body": "Widget Setup The Widget Setup tab controls the appearance, behavior, branding, and installation of the website chat widget. These settings determine how visitors experience the chatbot on your website. Appearance Brand Logo Upload your organization's logo. Supported Formats PNG JPG SVG Primary Color Used for: Header Buttons Interactive elements Secondary Color Used for: Secondary actions Accent elements Chat Bubble Color Color of visitor chat messages. Agent Message Color Color of chatbot or agent messages. Background Color Defines the chat window background. Font Family Supported options include: Default Inter Roboto DM Sans System Font Font Size Options: Small Medium Large Widget Launcher (Chat Bubble) Controls the chat icon displayed on the website. Launcher Type Options include: Chat Bubble Floating Button Text Button Custom Icon Custom Image Upload Allows administrators to upload a custom launcher icon. Launcher Text Examples: Chat with Us Need Help? Support Bubble Size Options: Small Medium Large Widget Position Controls where the chat widget appears. Available Positions Bottom Right Bottom Left Right Margin Distance from the right edge of the screen. Bottom Margin Distance from the bottom edge of the screen. Z Index Controls display priority when overlapping with website elements. Chat Window Layout Defines how the chat window is displayed. Chat Window Title Example: Support Chat Subtitle Example: We typically reply in a few minutes. Header Logo Optional logo displayed within the chat window. Window Size Options: Compact Medium Large Window Style Options: Rounded Minimal Card Style Chat Avatar Profile image displayed for chatbot messages. Chat Widget Behavior Auto Open Chat Window Automatically opens the chat window after a specified delay. Auto Show Bubble Displays the launcher bubble automatically after a configured time. Show Only After Scroll Displays the widget after visitors scroll for a specified percentage of the page. Show on Exit Intent Displays the widget when the visitor appears ready to leave the website. Welcome & Messages Welcome Message Displayed when the chat window first opens. Example: Hello! How can we help you today? Pre Chat Form Collects visitor information before a conversation begins. Enable Pre Chat Form When enabled, visitors may be asked to provide: Name Email Phone Number Company Custom Questions :::note This information can be used for lead generation and qualification. ::: Engagement Triggers Used to proactively engage website visitors. Proactive Message Example: Need help finding something? Trigger Conditions Messages can be triggered based on: Time spent on page Scroll percentage Number of pages visited Returning visitor status Mobile Experience Controls chatbot behavior on mobile devices. Mobile Widget Enabled Enable or disable the chatbot on mobile devices. Mobile Window Style Options: Full Screen Floating Chat Auto Open on Mobile Automatically opens the chatbot for mobile visitors. Sound & Notifications New Message Sound Plays a sound when a new message is received. Sound Types Ping Chime None Browser Notifications Displays browser based message notifications. Advanced Settings Persistent Chat Preserves conversations across page refreshes. Visitor Tracking Enabled Tracks visitor interactions across sessions. URL Rules Control where the chatbot appears. Examples: Show on all pages Show only on specific pages Hide on specific pages Installation Installation Script Administrators can copy the generated script and add it to their website. Domain Restriction Restrict widget usage to approved domains. Examples: company.com support.company.com",
