    "description": "Learn how to create and manage tags for organizing Knowledge Base content in Pulse Settings.",
    "body": "Tags The Tags feature allows administrators to create and manage tags specifically for organizing Knowledge Base content. Knowledge Base tags are managed separately under Pulse Settings → Tags and are independent of the tags used for CRM modules such as Leads, Deals, Contacts, and Organizations. Accessing Tags To manage Knowledge Base tags: 1. Go to Pulse Settings . 2. Select Tags . 3. The Tags page displays the available tags. 4. Click Create Tag to create a new tag. Tags List The Tags page displays the following information: Tag Name – Name of the tag. Usage Count – Number of Knowledge Base items using the tag. Status – Current status of the tag. Created By – User who created the tag. Created Date – Date the tag was created. Actions – Available actions for managing the tag. You can use the Search by tag name field to quickly find a specific tag. The available filters can also be used to filter tags by: Status Created By Created Date Creating a Tag To create a Knowledge Base tag: 1. Click Create Tag . 2. Enter the required tag details. 3. Save the tag. The tag can then be used to organize relevant Knowledge Base content. Example Knowledge Base tags can be used to categorize content such as: FAQs Troubleshooting Product Documentation Training Policies Release Notes :::note Tags created under Pulse Settings → Tags are specifically used for Knowledge Base content and are separate from CRM tags. :::",
