    "label": "Facebook Messenger & Instagram Integration",
    "title": "Facebook Messenger & Instagram Integration",
    "to": "/docs/PulseChannelIntegrations/FacebookMessenger&Instagram",
    "description": "Connect Facebook Messenger and Instagram to Pulse Channels using Meta authorization.",
    "body": "Facebook Messenger & Instagram Integration Overview The Facebook and Instagram channels allow CRM to receive and manage customer conversations from Facebook Messenger and Instagram Direct Messages within the Pulse Inbox. Once connected, incoming messages from both channels can be handled directly from the CRM without switching between Meta applications. Prerequisites Before connecting the channels, ensure that: You have a Facebook account. You have administrator access to the Facebook Page. Your Facebook Page has Messenger enabled. Your Instagram account is a Professional (Business or Creator) account. The Instagram account is linked to the Facebook Page. You have permission to manage both the Facebook Page and the Instagram account. The Facebook Page and the Instagram Professional account must not be owned by another Business Portfolio. Steps to Connect Facebook Messenger & Instagram Step 1: Navigate to the Channels Page Go to: Pulse Settings → Channels The Channels page displays all the available communication channels. Step 2: Connect Facebook Locate the Facebook channel and click Connect . :::note Connecting Facebook also connects the linked Instagram account automatically. A separate Instagram connection is not required. ::: Step 3: Sign in to Facebook A Meta authorization window appears. Sign in using the Facebook account that manages your Facebook Page and the linked Instagram Professional account. :::note A single Facebook account can be used to connect multiple Meta channels, including: WhatsApp Business Facebook Messenger Instagram Make sure the Facebook account you sign in with has administrator access to the Business Portfolio and the required business assets. ::: Step 4: Continue as Your Facebook Account After signing in, Meta displays a confirmation screen showing the Facebook account that will be used for the authorization. Review the displayed account information. Click Continue as Your Facebook Account to proceed. Step 5: Select the Facebook Page Meta displays the Facebook Pages that you manage. You can choose one of the following options: Opt in to all current and future Pages – Grants the CRM access to all your existing Pages and any Pages you create in the future. Opt in to current Pages only – Allows you to manually select the Facebook Page(s) you want to authorize. If you choose Opt in to current Pages only : 1. Select the checkbox next to the Facebook Page you want to connect. 2. Verify that the correct Facebook Page is selected. 3. Click Continue . :::note Only the selected Facebook Page(s) will be accessible to the CRM. ::: Step 6: Select the Business Account Meta now asks you to choose which Business Account(s) the CRM can access. You can choose one of the following options: Opt in to all current and future Businesses – Grants the CRM access to all your existing Business Accounts and any Business Accounts you create in the future. Opt in to current Businesses only – Allows you to manually select the Business Account(s) you want to authorize. If you select Opt in to current Businesses only : 1. Select the checkbox next to the Business Account you want to connect. 2. Verify that the correct Business Account is selected. 3. Click Continue . :::note Only the selected Business Account(s) will be accessible to the CRM. ::: Step 7: Select the Instagram Account Meta displays the Instagram account(s) associated with your Facebook Page. You can choose one of the following options: Opt in to all current and future Instagram accounts – Grants the CRM access to all your existing and future Instagram Professional accounts. Opt in to current Instagram accounts only – Allows you to manually select the Instagram account(s) you want to authorize. If you choose Opt in to current Instagram accounts only : 1. Select the checkbox next to the Instagram account you want to connect. 2. Verify that the correct Instagram account is selected. 3. Click Continue . :::note Only the selected Instagram account(s) will be connected to",
