    "body": "The User Management section is the central administrative area used to create, manage, and control user accounts within the CRM. It allows administrators to onboard users, assign roles and permissions, manage account access, and maintain organizational user information. User Management ensures that the right users have the appropriate level of access to CRM features, records, and modules while maintaining security, governance, and operational control. Purpose of User Management The User Management module helps organizations: Create and onboard users into the CRM Assign roles and permissions Manage user access to modules and features Maintain employee and organizational information Control account activation and deactivation Configure reporting managers and team assignments Enable secure authentication and access control Support organizational visibility structures Core Functionalities of User Management 1. User Creation & Onboarding 2. Role & Permission Assignment 3. Team Assignment 4. Reporting Hierarchy Assignment 5. Access & Visibility Control 6. Sharing Rules Management Key Benefits of User Management The User Management module helps organizations: Maintain secure access control Simplify employee onboarding Manage organizational structures efficiently Enable secure cross team collaboration Control permissions centrally Improve operational governance Enable scalable CRM administration The module is divided into three sections: 1. Users 2. Roles 3. Access 4. Security Let's explore each of them in detail.",
